WEBVTT

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.550
It goes without saying...

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.060
you cannot create magic with morality.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.750
Oh, well.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.300
Soon enough...

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.760
your dream will become reality.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.270
Because of me.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.770
You're welcome, professor.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.730
This is...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.030
What?

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.350
Sorry, we were out of tea.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.350
We only had instant coffee.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.360
Monica would often say...

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.320
how similar you were to her.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.090
When your emotions take control...

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.600
you lose sight of what you should do.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.190
That's something Monica would always...

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.110
I know full well that my emotions
are getting the better of me.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.530
I know they are.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.620
But I just can't believe Monica died
of a heart attack.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.120
We finally found a lead
with the LIVE Corporation.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.460
So...

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.510
how could I sit here and do nothing?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.170
I can't!

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.650
It may connect to Monica.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.540
What is this?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.880
Our people have been looking into them
for a long time.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.900
The LIVE Corporation.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:48.990
They've been the target
of many investigations,

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.240
but nobody has been able
to build a case against them.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.580
The closer we get to the truth,
the more clever they get.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.420
Monica discovered that LIVE
was connected to some allegation

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.550
and reached out to Fred.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.760
Or maybe the other way around.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.260
In other words, LIVE killed Monica?

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:21.020
How could they know what Monica was up to?

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.270
What are you saying?

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.860
She was being watched?

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.330
If someone was monitoring Monica
from close by,

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.830
and relayed it to LIVE...

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.540
Who could it be?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.590
Finding darkness in broad daylight...

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.100
it's tricky.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:08.820
Anything...

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.820
Whatever I have to do...

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.570
I'll do it.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:22.660
Sarah.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.000
We are a team.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.090
Don't forget that.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.630
Yes, sir.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:34.630
Whatever is hiding in the darkness...

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.800
I'll drag out into the open.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.680
Just remember,

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.100
be careful.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:58.950
Good night.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.000
Sarah.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:13.880
Don't worry,

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.340
I can do this.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.550
Now, then.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:05.890
I have a feeling...

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.730
this is going to be
a long and dark battle.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:14.860
<i>And we here at the LIVE Corporation</i>

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.950
<i>will work to make your lives better.</i>

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.240
<i>To assist you in your lives.</i>

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.330
<i>That is our mission.</i>

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.380
Get out of the way!

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.970
Did you miss me?

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.890
Okay, okay.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:52.230
<i>To offer the people the technology</i>
<i>we develop at the LIVE Corporation</i>

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.070
<i>that will help them in their daily lives,</i>

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:59.650
that is what our company is meant to be.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:04.160
Could you explain how your military
projects and humanitarian efforts coexist?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:09.210
Because they are both founded
on technology.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:13.080
Does that mean you are focusing on
technology to--?

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:16.130
Could you comment on the allegations
against you?

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:20.840
Wait!

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.190
Anna Winehouse.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.990
Steven Martland. You're looking well.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:48.080
I heard that Ecohes is close to finishing
a new drug.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.750
We have so many.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:00.550
To the success of Ecohes' new,
highly-anticipated drug,

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.930
and LIVE's welfare work.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.230
Oh, my, this drink.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.990
It smells of blood.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.030
And of gunpowder.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:42.170
For you it seems that
anyone who is not good

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.300
must be evil.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:48.100
At times,

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:52.560
people will turn to guns
rather than drugs.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.990
It was an honor to see you.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.650
The honor was mine.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:39.770
<i>James.</i>

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.530
Turn your contacts on,
or I can't give you support.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.900
<i>Yeah, I know.</i>

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.040
You're sure this is the place?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.460
Yes, Fred Faraday used to live here.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.600
A card reader.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.100
Okay, hold on, I'll try--

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.640
<i>The kitchen doesn't look like</i>
<i>it's been used.</i>

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.900
This date...

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.660
November 5th.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.020
What is it?

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:55.830
The drain?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:58.040
So, the noise is coming from the basement?

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:17.390
Be careful.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.030
Wolf!

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.160
You scared me.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:38.050
I guess your owner hasn't been home
in a while, huh?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:39.780
Eddy.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.280
I'm on it.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.040
She looks familiar.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.120
Got it. Sending it over.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.550
"Anna Winehouse"?

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.550
This woman is the president of Ecohes.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.550
Ecohes, the pharmaceutical company?

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:03.850
Yeah.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.060
They've had a string
of new drug announcements lately.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.940
Fred and Anna.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.850
<i>-What?</i>
-Never mind.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:20.950
"Future and responsibility
of pharmaceuticals"?

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:22.700
James,

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:25.200
<i>it seems she's giving a lecture tonight.</i>

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:32.380
Okay.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:09.540
I see.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:14.920
While I had anticipated this,
I didn't think it would be you.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.090
The grim reaper of LIVE Corporation,

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.430
Harry Creighton.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:30.140
I saw you at the hospital once
by coincidence.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:38.400
You put all of your considerable payments
towards a certain woman.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:45.870
She's very beautiful.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:03.090
If you wish to save her,
then you should choose a different way.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.760
Something much more effective...

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.890
and much more absolute.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.150
Do you still not understand?

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.980
I'm talking about the Masks.

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:23.900
The Masks?

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:29.030
I hope you don't think
the Masks I created are just weapons.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:37.540
Take a look.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.390
<i>In order to conquer diseases,</i>

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:54.390
<i>we cut people open to perform surgery.</i>

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:59.150
<i>What enabled this bold new idea</i>
<i>was anesthetics.</i>

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:03.070
Ecohes.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.610
In other words,
medication must be something

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:12.120
that rapidly expands the possibility
of medical science.

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:14.410
What is demanded

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:17.920
is challenge and inspiration
that far exceeds the imagination.

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:23.300
And we researchers must have
wisdom and courage.

00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:45.110
Anna Winehouse.

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:21.870
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
